<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shamash-resha-usur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shamash-resha-usur was a governor of Suhu and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mari">Mari</a> on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> in the first half of the 8th century BCE, nominally subject to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>. His Akkadian inscriptions describe canal building and fighting off raiders, and one stela records that he brought honeybees from the mountains of the Habha people and learned to make honey and wax, the earliest known account of beekeeping in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. His son Ninurta-kudurri-usur succeeded him.</p></div>
